; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- user interface

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=The 2htm dialog: its fields, its underlined letters, and the keys that work anywhere in it, each shown as the reader speaks it.
Setup=2htm installed; the dialog open with Alt+Control+2.
Homework=Open the dialog, press F7, choose a control from the list, then press Shift+F1 there to hear its tip.

[step]

Say=One want: to move around the 2htm dialog without hunting. Everything in it can be reached by a letter.
Key=

[step]

Say=I press the desktop key for 2htm. The dialog opens on its first field.
Key=Alt+Control+2
Hear=2htm dialog
Hear=Source files edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Source files names what to convert: one file, a folder, a pattern such as star dot docx, or several with spaces between. Its letter is S.
Key=

[step]

Say=Tab moves to the next control, a button that opens a file picker.
Key=Tab
Hear=Browse source button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every label has an underlined letter, and Alt with that letter jumps straight to it. Output directory is O.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Output directory edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Left blank, each web page is written beside its document. Choose output, C, picks a folder instead of typing one.
Key=

[step]

Say=Then the check boxes. Force replacements, F, replaces a web page already made; without it, a document whose page exists is skipped.
Key=Alt+F
Hear=Force replacements check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Plain text, P, makes a text file instead of a web page.
Key=Alt+P
Hear=Plain text check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Strip images, I, leaves out the pictures.
Key=Alt+I
Hear=Strip images check box, not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=View output, V, opens the folder when the run is done; Log session, L, writes a log beside the output; Use configuration, U, remembers these choices for next time.
Key=

[step]

Say=Space checks a box and Space again clears it.
Key=Space
Hear=checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Not sure what something does? Shift plus F1 says the tip for the control you are on.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=Strip images: leave pictures out of the output
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F1 shows Help: every control with its tip, and every key.
Key=F1
Hear=2htm Help dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes Help and returns to the same place.
Key=Escape
Hear=Strip images check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space clears the box again, as I found it.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F7 lists every control in the dialog; choose one and press Enter to move there.
Key=F7
Hear=Controls list
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose Source files.
Key=Enter
Hear=Source files edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter starts converting from any field, and Control plus Enter does the same from any control. Escape closes the dialog without converting.
Key=Tab
Hear=Browse source button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Two more buttons sit at the end. Guide, G, opens the full guide in the browser and returns here; Default settings, D, clears every field and box.
Key=Alt+G
Hear=Guide button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The text fields remember your answers. In Source files, Up Arrow brings back what you typed last time, and earlier answers above it.
Key=Up Arrow
Hear=C colon backslash Documents backslash Annual Report dot docx
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow returns toward an empty field, so a fresh entry is a key or two away.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Source files edit, blank
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every label you hear is the control's own name, read once by the screen reader; 2htm adds speech only for what the reader cannot know, such as progress during a long run.
Key=

[step]

Say=That is the whole dialog: what to convert, where it goes, five boxes, and a key for everything. The next walk installs 2htm.
Key=
